// J. Sky and dates. Route: #/sky (?p=<screen, 1-based>). One traditional date per screen: what tradition or the source
// says, the night sky of that date drawn by the site (the Moon's phase and place, the tithi's place in its fortnight),
// then what the computation gives, with its assumptions and the other readings a tap away.
// Data: ./sky.js, generated by tools/build_sky.py (PyEphem, offline) from life.json date_claims: every input, convention,
// validation case and result. Nothing here computes astronomy; it only draws and words what the generator wrote.
// A computation is shown as a computation (mark status "reconstruction"), never as the answer to a dispute: the page says
// "agrees" or "does not agree" of a source's own parts, never "correct" or "wrong".
